<title>UK: KfW prices 1.5 billion mark seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>KfW prices 1.5 billion mark seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced Tuesday by joint lead managers Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and Commerzbank, has now been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KREDITANSTALT FUER WIEDERAUFBAU</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN DEM   COUPON     5.50	MATURITY    17.OCT.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.422    PAY DATE    17.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.25	REOFFER    99.422    SPREAD	+14 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   MGT/UND    0.30</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND SEPTEMBER 2003</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
